        },
        "TextSection": {
            "TextSectionType": "Definition",
            "Contents": "A group of rare disorders characterized by brachydactyly due to abnormal development of the phalanges and/or metacarpals. Brachydactyly is part of a group of limb malformations characterized by dysostosis involving abnormal development of individual bones either in isolation or in combination with other skeletal abnormalities. These disorders primarily affect the skeleton although extraskeletal manifestations may also occur."
        },
